      "title": "Structure and components",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "OIDC Core defines an ID token as a JWT describing authentication and requires issuer, subject, audience, and expiration claims. Google service-account ID tokens use those fields, but this general token structure is not proof of support for every Atlas login flow. (high confidence) Sources: https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html ; https://cloud.google.com/docs/authentication/token-types",
