    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Workforce setup requires a public/native OIDC application, JWT tokens rather than opaque tokens, and user or group mappings to database privileges. MongoDB recommends Authorization Code with PKCE; Device Authorization is the alternative for machines without browsers. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workforce-oidc.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f114ba770d6a9c6ca6ac47a4169a5a1144d7716b669ac1e8bfdab0ca0fa03b9c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2dc41713a565d4d854dd65ff30fe6e7b4fdceee6c8da6f7525f22619438b5184",
            "ev:915b5b85ead67f21869030d8bfdb523c5b1520d410ffc2b7bbf5789226cfddbc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the Google service-account path, register the numeric service-account Unique Id as the federated database user identifier, rather than the service-account email; the token subject identifies that account. (high confidence) Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md ; https://docs.cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/verifying-instance-identity",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
