    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas distinguishes Workforce Identity Federation for human database users using OIDC from Workload Identity Federation for applications using external programmatic identities, including GCP service accounts. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-oidc.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a1d6f49768547357d1da3e59bdeb33ff174af0df6519c79676180e0770e231b4",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:341eb0d853e16d290e87b8c6f7067c07d0c2b757ed824fbc35b63b9e2731f2fc"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workforce-oidc.md",
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workforce-oidc/?fresh=20261023",
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The cached Atlas setup guides restrict both federation paths to dedicated clusters (M10 and above) running MongoDB 7.0.11 or later; this is narrower than generic references to MongoDB 7.0 support. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14) Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workforce-oidc.md ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workforce-oidc.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:04bba20de9706729ce6f33427689d6b9ce66c8d71c85a7e024500d2475c33344",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workforce-oidc/?fresh=20261023",
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/"
          ],
          "originValidationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "originEvidenceIds": [
            "ev:5d25d42d05875665816a730f72f2634f611f17a2ebee209908bb486f8b54204a",
            "ev:b3da70b16493caa715fa2f832236c8edfc5459d59b42cd1afde3eb22cdc51479"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1",
            "record": "remediation.json",
            "requires_revalidation": true,
            "claim_text_sha256": "6079238ffeb3d4621ba8d4b6c2c30a937a8f37de84fa92f593f73623a1a7e9dd"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Workload federation lets a supported driver obtain a token for the runtime identity and present it to Atlas without a database password. Atlas still stores the identity-to-privilege mapping; federation does not remove database authorization configuration. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:14430dfb453e82cab867f299d7a76071e5b94f4e23106309815d10816480c9b7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:16dc3ee1f6eb911e726aa896550c04671f43a31ed28cbe8edbc823aa1232b548",
            "ev:8d064c86ddecd41c444703a88833b3f5f1bcc2c2417d8cb93234c2af24a3cd6f"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://medium.com/google-cloud/passwordless-between-google-cloud-and-mongodb-atlas-36701c0c5d17"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For GCP metadata-service authentication, configure MONGODB-OIDC with ENVIRONMENT=gcp and TOKEN_RESOURCE set to the configured audience. PyMongo documents built-in support for Compute Engine or another runtime that exposes the GCP metadata service. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/security/authentication/oidc/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1b030f789e3fcf7dedf2e6e424d473efcbfc661489df16e28e1d98cebdb8f24d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0a49cf3be99a445d4a5a25ff73b9c38b6d7507df389dee2a9ca215908063c338",
            "ev:e8674502063d434d1e4a8fd80884e738c86f1b2cfce7a7e6de42b0ac0bc4e841"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://medium.com/google-cloud/passwordless-between-google-cloud-and-mongodb-atlas-36701c0c5d17",
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "On the MongoDB Go driver’s master branch, client-option validation for MONGODB-OIDC rejects a nonempty password and simultaneous human and machine callbacks. If ENVIRONMENT is “gcp,” it requires a nonempty TOKEN_RESOURCE. These validation errors can occur before server authentication. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-22)",
          "source": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-go-driver/blob/master/mongo/options/clientoptions.go",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9e3a7fcf8c47e1519aa44de9458ea543bb6eb4c0ca323c675a7f6653d61ca778",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:7794609c1553660a6cf58775355e2fdfa750ddba2a715ac2459a4a580e0afdf0",
            "ev:d1cc7a8c573ffe28c1052c1dbbf3eb70bcb82a72f45349aab276a5016dad5f24"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo-go-driver/blob/master/x/mongo/driver/auth/oidc.go"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Google recommends avoiding service account keys whenever possible, attaching a service account to the resource when running in Google Cloud, or using Workload Identity Federation for workloads on-premises or on other clouds. The MongoDB Node.js driver has built-in GCP Instance Metadata Service OIDC support, so on Compute Engine an application can authenticate to MongoDB without a downloaded service-account key. Sources: https://docs.cloud.google.com/iam/docs/best-practices-service-accounts ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/security/authentication/oidc.md",
          "source": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/iam/docs/best-practices-service-accounts",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b654a922c6a69fc9c3b9a28aac62f84a820d72fd928632e2d7c18ee4c6575b85",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/drivers/node/current/security/authentication/oidc.md"
          ],
          "originValidationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "originEvidenceIds": [
            "ev:5b1c1ceaf05f61fe3848ac716e4141f943853221f086b136b4f93fcdff6d16ff",
            "ev:7077bc4d60764b58c0a30fcfd460af658d36a1d92b6496c985ae44e5be294005"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1",
            "record": "remediation.json",
            "requires_revalidation": true,
            "claim_text_sha256": "4646b07ea3518146222c38dd369ab58fd8767c94d445e5728c573a4bbbb62678"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Google Cloud incoming Workload Identity Federation and Atlas database federation are separate trust configurations. GitHub documents exchanging a GitHub OIDC token to access Google Cloud; Atlas requires its own identity provider and database privilege mapping. Configuring the former alone does not configure Atlas access. (medium confidence) Sources: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/secure-your-work/security-harden-deployments/oidc-in-google-cloud-platform ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
          "source": "https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/secure-your-work/security-harden-deployments/oidc-in-google-cloud-platform",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:960f86657ededdc33838a81ab98a57d27e69191ef0b7ab3f82cc0c87c3552080",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
            "https://docs.cloud.google.com/iam/docs/best-practices-service-accounts"
          ],
          "originValidationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "originEvidenceIds": [
            "ev:8d064c86ddecd41c444703a88833b3f5f1bcc2c2417d8cb93234c2af24a3cd6f",
            "ev:a73ca13202eba3143c1b51105a3a63651d2a223b138f619e373f1b311627fe64"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1",
            "record": "remediation.json",
            "requires_revalidation": true,
            "claim_text_sha256": "fbfd1d30c8a4636a0a74de6cc6b4895be57a2c8bc937eb8b6ed0b8b0cc6baa6c"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "For a GCP application connection, the Atlas database user or group identifier for Workload Identity Federation maps to the Unique Id of the GCP Service Account, and database privileges are assigned as a separate step when adding the user or group. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:31c6ce859a6bf95c8dd28c57877029d0412a8c356ca5b9cfd7037b5546309f36",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://medium.com/google-cloud/passwordless-between-google-cloud-and-mongodb-atlas-36701c0c5d17"
          ],
          "originValidationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "originEvidenceIds": [
            "ev:ddef403564cd2d934255a0a034eceba4e06823b458ce58b9d915d9e2aa17f79d",
            "ev:e3df2637839f3c3aeb820266882dbe666e0ce0fd7e3eab68adf83fa56d491baf"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1",
            "record": "remediation.json",
            "requires_revalidation": true,
            "claim_text_sha256": "3f88bc70b90995fc721539eac9909f271e4ba2c2c5bf9fcb5c3e829a82254bea"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "For workforce access, Atlas requires MongoDB Shell or Compass. Workload Identity Federation is supported only by selected drivers. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workforce-oidc.md ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workforce-oidc.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d0760660fa1a0e3d2d3d959b29e873aa233f8490e31cca333390d66e4392d640",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/"
          ],
          "originValidationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "originEvidenceIds": [
            "ev:619b51555a5c69b9d4f64e1653d1ff04381044c0e5e94682a29f221a55a23371",
            "ev:6fa8251b306fa0ea538c5d4540148aef2459660708bd5c5bcc6731ca5ccedf86"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1",
            "record": "remediation.json",
            "requires_revalidation": true,
            "claim_text_sha256": "80b4b08192a2f02a92796fdb2a4ea0c2e7a161272c2b92347951f2859315b0a7"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "For GCP workloads, keep the Atlas user claim as the default sub, and map the database user identifier to the Unique Id of the GCP service account. Google's Compute Engine instance identity tokens use https://accounts.google.com as the issuer and the service account's unique ID as the subject. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/ ; https://docs.cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/verifying-instance-identity",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:dce2e17285bd8fe2a28193cf8482e9590c4c5440584dbec2f7251651091240db",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://docs.cloud.google.com/docs/authentication/token-types",
            "https://docs.cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/verifying-instance-identity"
          ],
          "originValidationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "originEvidenceIds": [
            "ev:c325b6257a099f075e463ce7e7a830c9ad6376c052e196179ecbf03294b64cf4",
            "ev:d59a950dea2c705294daffd7dc8aca04d12518a68c6a56881590484dffc84953"
          ],
          "remediation": {
            "schema": "claim-remediation-projection/v1",
            "record": "remediation.json",
            "requires_revalidation": true,
            "claim_text_sha256": "3307d8aee08eb7f927296e5c02475d0733654fb3147a4313a8adc78a0e090b2a"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas offers built-in metadata authentication and application-provided token callbacks. The callback must obtain a suitable token; federation does not remove the need to configure identity trust and database privileges. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a8a8a5fa01e2a122665beac1221098ebc6b181a7cfcc1afd17bd60ff3de62b5a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:09baf1b3e7e2c9a06ca0dadea827465ab84902f12cd0cb11c10c8954bb97c7d9",
            "ev:6850c0457046035f1354bdd8daa4549e6aea555cbd3a8966564fc74994f4c490"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/languages/python/pymongo-driver/current/security/authentication/oidc/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "An Atlas workload provider becomes available across projects in its connected organization, but administrators must still add federated database identities and assign privileges. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:246eac4805bd1f9ce2557f87f7654ce34de357ae0865b92b139306fb4be5124a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:fc1e77f911611d9632201fee0801dc9b32a9471c46de92f3a3137fb77a8ef419"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas lists Compute Engine, App Engine, Cloud Functions, Cloud Run, GKE, and Cloud Build as GCP infrastructure supporting built-in workload authentication. Check the chosen driver and runtime before deployment. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:dc8d27d955b505488b8fd184ba10fa1db28f32b6bc57b1e9e38f03166c351b0d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:d7c2922a5680e4cbdb1aace7620a5e88ef44dffb76d8f9be4b391d6bc62232cb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Google Cloud IAM Workload Identity Federation exchanges external credentials for access to Google Cloud resources. Atlas workload federation instead authenticates applications to MongoDB. Treat these as separate trust configurations; a Google IAM pool alone does not establish Atlas database access. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23) Sources: https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/workload-identity-federation ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/workload-oidc.md",
          "source": "https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/workload-identity-federation",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1f7b4980e002873f6a387c57df3e58e4cd35451721977fbb8cdc6b547ef8e72d",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
